hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1122","Saeed bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Makhzoumi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Salem Abi Al-Nadr, on the authority of Abu Salama bin Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of Aisha She said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray the two rak’ahs of dawn. If I was awake, he would speak to me, and if I was asleep, he would lie down until He stands for prayer.”"
